    Add custom URLStreamHandlerFactory support to Fetch API
    
    This adds the ability to set a custom URLStreamHandlerFactory on Fetch
    and pass it down to CacheUrl for custom protocol resolution, while
    maintaining backward compatibility with existing classloader-based
    protocol resolution.
    
    Key changes:
    - Add customHandlerFactory parameter to CacheUrl.url() with fallback logic
    - Extend ConnectionBuilder, Downloader, FileCache, and Fetch to accept and pass URLStreamHandlerFactory
    - Custom handler factory is tried first, falls back to existing classloader resolution
    - All existing functionality preserved - 87/87 cache tests pass
    - Add comprehensive tests for new functionality
    
    The implementation allows users to provide custom protocol handlers at the
    API level without modifying global state or requiring classloader manipulation.
    
